//? Title: Marching squares contour segments
//? Subtitle: Actual crossed-edge interpolation, explicit saddle topology and the original radial field
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Marching squares classifies four grid-cell corners and connects interpolated
edge crossings. We retain the original21-by21 radial field and radius-six
midpoint observations, expose actual cell/interpolation records, and make the
formerly implicit saddle connectivity explicit. Returned segments are
independent cell pieces, not a stitched exact level-set certificate.
)

\toc

> Tiny classified cell and real crossed edges

Grid column is x and row is y. Corner bits1,2,4,8 correspond to
row0-left,row0-right,row1-right,row1-left. A corner is above when its sample is
at least the finite requested level; equality therefore belongs to the above
class. An edge crosses only when its two endpoint classifications differ. For a
crossed edge with samples f_a,f_b, the interpolation fraction is
t=(iso−f_a)/(f_b−f_a), and its point is p_a+t*(p_b−p_a).

For rows[1,0] and[0,0] at level0.5, only row0-left is above, giving case1. The
actual crossed edges are row0 horizontal and column0 vertical, at(0.5,0)
and(0,0.5). The method connects those native points. The old implementation
evaluated every cell edge, including unused constant edges with a zero
denominator; the new producer interpolates only genuinely crossed edges.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/marching_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::marching_squares_trace({{1, 0}, {0, 0}}, .5);
    std::print("| actual edge0:row0,1:col1,2:row1,3:col0 | actual first sample | actual second sample | " "actual fraction | actual x | actual y |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &c : t.crossings)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", c.edge, c.first_value,
                   c.second_value, c.fraction, c.point[0], c.point[1]);
    auto &s = t.analysis.segments.front();
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("grid", {0, 0}, "Actual original samples\nrow0[1,0], row1[0,0]").node("mask", {6, 0}, std::format("Actual corner case{}\nreal crossed edges{}", t.cells.front().case_index, t.crossings.size())).node("segment", {12, 0}, std::format("Actual segment endpoints\n({},{}) to({},{})", s[0], s[1], s[2], s[3])).edge("grid", "mask").edge("mask", "segment");
    d.save_svg("build/marching_tiny.svg");
}
```
