> Original radial field and measured circle deviations

Retain21 samples per axis, center(10,10), values sqrt((column−10)^2+(row−10)^2),
and level6. The native study owns that exact prescribed field, extracts the
actual44 segments using the historical saddle rule, and measures absolute radial
deviation at each returned segment midpoint. The original mean near0.0215291 and
maximum near0.0279425 are observations at those finitely many midpoints, not a
uniform contour-error bound or a topology certificate.

Both numeric coordinate axes use the same range and physical scale, so the
contour’s geometry is not stretched into an ellipse. The native segment list is
plotted directly; no report-local field sampler, contour extractor,
midpoint-error routine or reconstructed analytic circle supplies the figure.
This synthetic field has a known exact reference and needs no external dataset.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/marching_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto s = dm::algorithms::marching_radial_study();
    std::print("Actual grid{} by{}; actual segments {}; measured midpoint observations {}; actual mean " "radial deviation {}; actual maximum radial deviation {}.\n\n| actual segment index | actual " "x0 | actual y0 | actual x1 | actual y1 | actual midpoint radial deviation |\n| ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               s.grid.size(), s.grid.front().size(), s.contour.segments.size(),
               s.midpoint_errors.size(), s.mean_midpoint_error,
               s.maximum_midpoint_error);
    std::vector<double> x0, y0, x1, y1;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < s.contour.segments.size(); ++i) {
        auto &v = s.contour.segments[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, v[0], v[1], v[2],
                   v[3], s.midpoint_errors[i]);
        x0.push_back(v[0]);
        y0.push_back(v[1]);
        x1.push_back(v[2]);
        y1.push_back(v[3]);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.segments(x0, y0, x1, y1, {37, 99, 235}, 2).size(850, 850).margins(95, 35,
                                                                        60, 70).x_limits(0, 20).y_limits(0, 20).title("Original radial field: actual44 contour segments").x_label("grid column x").y_label("grid row y").save_svg("build/marching_original.svg");
}
```
