> Alternating corners require an explicit topology choice

Cases5 and10 have alternating above/below corners and four edge crossings. The
crossings alone permit two pairings. The historical fixed rule isolates the
above corners: case5 connects left-to-row0 and right-to-row1, while case10 uses
row0-to-right and left-to-row1. The default AboveDisconnected preserves those
exact original pairs and their order. The new explicit AboveConnected option
chooses the alternative two pairs in each saddle.

Neither fixed rule is a bilinear asymptotic decider. Sample magnitudes can
change the interior bilinear saddle topology while leaving the four corner signs
and boundary crossings unchanged. The API exposes the user’s connectivity choice
rather than implying the original fixed rule resolves every continuous level-set
ambiguity. The paired diagrams show actual native segments for the same case5
grid, with row zero drawn above row one for matrix readability. Their geometry
is derived solely from the actual segment coordinates and corner values.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/marching_saddles.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;
    node.width = .7;
    node.height = .7;
    node.font_size = 16;
    node.padding = 2;
    node.circle = true;
    std::print("| actual saddle rule0:above-disconnected,1:above-connected | actual segment index | actual " "x0 | actual y0 | actual x1 | actual y1 |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (int policy = 0; policy < 2; ++policy) {
        auto rule =
            policy ? dm::algorithms::MarchingSaddleConnectivity::AboveConnected
            : dm::algorithms::MarchingSaddleConnectivity::AboveDisconnected;
        auto t =
            dm::algorithms::marching_squares_trace({{1, 0}, {0, 1}}, .5, rule);
        double offset = 9. * policy;
        d.text({offset + 2.5, 1.2},
               policy ? "Actual above connected" : "Actual above disconnected",
               18);
        d.path({{offset, 0}, {offset + 5, 0}, {offset + 5, -5}, {offset, -5},
                {offset, 0}});
        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.analysis.segments.size(); ++i) {
            auto &s = t.analysis.segments[i];
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", policy, i, s[0],
                       s[1], s[2], s[3]);
            dm::graphics::DiagramStroke stroke;
            stroke.color =
                policy ? dm::graphics::RGB{220, 38, 38}
                : dm::graphics::RGB{37, 99, 235};
            stroke.width = 3;
            d.path({{offset + 5 * s[0], -5 * s[1]},
                    {offset + 5 * s[2], -5 * s[3]}}, stroke);
        }
        std::array<double, 4> x{0, 5, 5, 0}, y{0, 0, -5, -5};
        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
            d.node(std::format("p{}_{}", policy, i), {offset + x[i], y[i]},
                   std::format("{}", t.cells.front().values[i]), node);
    }
    d.text({7, -6.2},
           "Actual columns increase right; displayed rows increase downward", 17);
    d.save_svg("build/marching_saddles.svg");
}
```
